    "title": "MACE (4-component major adverse cardiovascular events) definition in ESPRESSO",
    "source": "ESPRESSO Study; MACE_definitions_ESPRESSO_261103.docx",
    "version": "2026-11-03 (based on discussion with Johan Sundström, 2026-10-13)",
    "last_updated": "2026-11-03",
    "description": "Ischaemic heart disease, heart failure, stroke and CV death (ICD-8/9/10), with prior-CVD exclusion. specificity 'high' marks the codes shown in red in the source document (extra high specificity). Heart failure ICD-8 codes use a decimal comma as in the source. The register for the three Patient Register outcome components is assumed to be the Patient Register.",
    "used_in": [
      "MC and CVD (Forss, Clin Gastroenterol Hepatol 2023)",
      "EoE and CVD (Forss, Aliment Pharmacol Ther 2023)",
      "Diverticular disease and MACE (Forss, in revision)",
      "NAFLD and MACE in adults (Simon, Gut 2021)",
      "CVD in GI cancer survivors (manuscript submitted, Yin Cao)",
      "MACE by IBD drug therapy (Eriksson/Forss, ECCO abstract)"
    ],
    "limits": "Heart failure is a soft endpoint; CV death defined as all of Chapter I is broad; the stroke range changes between ICD-8/9 and ICD-10.",
    "sensitivity_analyses": "MI and stroke subtypes"
  },
